# Stray empty directory produced by a driver probe on Windows
NVIDIA Corporation/

# Dev-set review artifacts. Regenerate with the documented commands instead of
# versioning megabytes of contact sheets and overlay renders:
#   python tools/make_previews.py --video <clip> --out-dir previews/w39 --start 38 --end 42 --every 0.5
#   python tools/scan_motion.py  --video <clip> --out-dir reports/scan
previews/
labels_preview/
debug/*.png
debug/*.csv
debug/*.mp4

# Weights.
#
# The 109 MB YOLO11x checkpoint IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE. Grading is offline, so
# weights/download.sh cannot be relied on to run at scoring time, and a missing
# weight file is a silent total loss: every frame returns zero detections, every
# video is submitted with an empty event list, Score_A = Score_B = 0, and
# `evaluate.py --validate-only` still reports VALID. Shipping the file makes the
# outcome correct whether the submission travels as a git clone or as a copy of
# the directory. 109 MB is far inside the 5 GB cap.
#
# No rule above matches *.pt, so the file is tracked by default; the explicit
# negation below keeps that true even if a blanket *.pt rule is added later.
# (A pattern containing an inner slash is anchored to this file's directory,
# which is why the negation is written with an explicit weights/ prefix.)
!weights/yolo11x.pt
